==Restrictions==
Max # of Deployable Cats: 1

==Battleground==
*1 [[Teacher Bun Bun]] spawns as the boss after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.
*1 [[Red EnerG]] spawns as the boss after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
*1 [[Alpacky]] spawns as the boss.
*Infinite [[Assassin Bear]]s spawn after 900 seconds<sup>27,000f</sup>, delay 900 seconds<sup>27,000f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Due to the presence of Red EnerG and Teacher Bun Bun, beating this stage before Stories of Legend with specialist ubers is quite hard. Fortunately, the Red EnerG and Teacher Bun Bun aren't particularly strong here.

==='''Recommended Units''''===
*[[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] - Can juggle Teacher Bun Bun by exchanging hits with him.
*[[Miter Saw Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Miter Saw Cat]] - Resistant to Aliens with Massive Damage to them, a single Miter Saw can easily ward off Alpacky for extended periods. In it's true form, it can even solo the alpacky, though this effectively requires [[An Ancient Curse]] to be beaten.
*[[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]] - Seafarer cat can act as an alternative to the true form of miter saw cat, has he can stall the alpacky and a few of them can beat it, though it does take a long time and if you have bad luck you can lose, a maxed freeze up talent is heavily recommended if you choose to do this strategy. Just make sure to bring the regular cat cannon in case the alpacky kills your seafarer after it strengthens.
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] - A fast, decent rusher with Massive Damage to Reds, Courier's Long Distance isn't that much of a concern as Red EnerG has even more range, allowing well-timed hits to very quickly tear him away.
*[[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] - With a level 40 Awakened Bahamut Cat using 2 Attack Up (Sm) [[Cat Combo]]s or 1 Attack Up (L) Cat Combo and his Explosion Talent, you can juggle the Red EnerG and BunBun to easily beat this stage.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Kai (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Kai μ]] - Being Resistant Floating with very high damage and health at the cost of range, Kai is one of the best answers to Teacher Bun Bun, with a cooldown short enough to replace when lost if she somehow could not solo him.
*[[Hattori Hanzo (Uber Rare Cat)|Immortal Hanzo]] - a level 30 Immortal Hanzo semi-reliably takes care of Teacher Bun Bun alone due to his Massive Damage and Freeze against Floating, especially with a Unit Attack Up Cat Combo, though this also requires [[An Ancient Curse]] to be beaten.

